1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,034
The year 2045. Genesis activates for the last
time.

2
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:07,967
No way! You're back!

3
00:00:07,987 --> 00:00:08,867
We did it.

4
00:00:08,887 --> 00:00:09,765
And the Earth?

5
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:17,904
They move closer to the window. The oceans are
blue again. The forests have regained their

6
00:00:17,924 --> 00:00:20,591
green. The atmosphere looks cleaner.

7
00:00:20,611 --> 00:00:22,436
Is that… our planet?

8
00:00:22,456 --> 00:00:24,052
Yes. Our home.

9
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:40,744
The historical records have changed.
Communities managed to adapt, protect their

10
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:44,740
ecosystems and reduce the risks that
threatened their future.

11
00:00:45,383 --> 00:00:51,500
In the ravine towns, people rehearsed which
way to climb. In the river cities, they kept

12
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:57,847
the riverbed clear. In the schools, children
went back to the playground. In the mountains,

13
00:00:57,867 --> 00:00:59,680
the siren sounded in time.

14
00:01:07,383 --> 00:01:15,560
Today the river rose. The siren sounded and we
all climbed the hill, just like we practiced.

15
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:23,777
My grandma says the river used to warn us. Now
we warn each other. There's school on Monday.

16
00:01:24,683 --> 00:01:32,645
You didn't save everything. Nobody can. Some
houses are gone. But the people are still here.

17
00:01:37,683 --> 00:01:38,833
So can we go?

18
00:01:38,853 --> 00:01:40,075
This time, yes.

19
00:01:41,317 --> 00:01:46,328
The planet never needed heroes who could
travel through time. It needed people willing

20
00:01:46,348 --> 00:01:47,635
to change the present.

21
00:01:48,035 --> 00:01:53,990
You don't have a machine to go back in time.
You don't need one. It's still today.

22
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:59,661
The Earth's data already exists: satellites
watching the planet every day, a second source

23
00:01:59,681 --> 00:02:05,982
to check them and, said out loud, what is
still unknown. Change begins when you go out
and share it.

24
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:25,640
TERRA 2045. A Los Causas Espaciales project
for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
